    "description": "Given the input:\n\n<\nhtml\n>\n\n<\nhead\n>\n\n<\nstyle\n\n/>\n\n<!-- < - - this is the culprit -->\n\n</\nhead\n>\n\n<\nbody\n>\n\n<\np\n>\nWhatever\n</\np\n>\n\n</\nbody\n>\n\n</\nhtml\n>\n\nJSoup 1.8.2 and also \nhttp://try.jsoup.org/~lJwWpjXYUSTBeBZhdEnS3Mt56g4\nwill produce:\n\n<\nhtml\n>\n\n<\nhead\n>\n\n<\nstyle\n>\n</\nstyle\n>\n\n</\nhead\n>\n\n<\nbody\n>\n\n&lt;/head&gt; &lt;body&gt; &lt;p&gt;Whatever&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/body&gt; &lt;/html&gt;\n\n</\nbody\n>\n\n</\nhtml\n>\n\nWith \n<title/>\ninstead of \n<style/>\n, the result is different but still wrong (\nhttp://try.jsoup.org/~BZ3uoMki-r904fZxUOWJgLJO7r8\n):\n\n<\nhtml\n>\n\n<\nhead\n>\n\n<\ntitle\n>\n</\ntitle\n>\n\n</\nhead\n>\n\n<\nbody\n>\n\n&lt;/head&gt; \n\n<\np\n>\nWhatever\n</\np\n>\n\n</\nbody\n>\n\n</\nhtml\n>\n\nThat weirdness was fixed for \n<script>\nwith Issue \n#305\n: \nhttp://try.jsoup.org/~3Ms6TQCrrdaA_uPgxgURYYvwFAg\n\n<\nhtml\n>\n\n<\nhead\n>\n\n<\nscript\n>\n</\nscript\n>\n\n</\nhead\n>\n\n<\nbody\n>\n\n<\np\n>\nWhatever\n</\np\n>\n\n</\nbody\n>\n\n</\nhtml\n>\n\nLooking \nat the source\n, it seems only the HtmlTreeBuilderState handling for \n<noframes>\n, \n<style>\nand \n<title>\nin the methods \nhandleRawText\nand \nhandleRcData\ndoesn't get along with the self-closing tags.\n\nAny other tagname I've checked (and I tried to cover all branches of that \ncase StartTag\nswitch) results in a good parse similar to the \n<script>\ncase, which is what I'd expect.\n\nThanks for looking into this!"
